      "title": "Profiled glass",
      "summary": "Profiled glass is cast glass produced in a U-shaped profile, translucent and ornamented on the outside surface. It has low maintenance requirements and is used for lift shafts and roof glazing; fenestration using it is described as glare-free. The page presents profile types, installation possibilities, physical data, opening-height tables, installation dimensions, curved forms, and bending examples. Reglit and Profilit products are described as fire-glass with class G30; profiles with longitudinal wires are also available.",
